            "title": "Talent, writing and review",
            "body": "· pages 28–29\n\nThe reading asks whether talent is **innate** (present from birth) or shaped by **nurture** (training and environment). The written preview supports facts about Carissa Yip; the video-dependent questions require the missing video. For speaking, build a claim, give an example, acknowledge another view, and conclude.\n\nThe final writing task is a **200–220-word opinion summary**. State your position clearly, select two or three main reasons, and end with a concise conclusion. The source example discusses children learning music; its claims about intelligence are presented as claims in the text, not as verified scientific facts.\n\n## 2.5 Lookback · page 30 and reference pages\n\nReview learning expressions, hypothetical past, opinion collocations, verb patterns, and opinion introductions. Language Bank pages **130–131** contain the grammar reference and practice; Vocabulary Bank page **149** expands metaphors and opinion collocations. Page **159** provides the partner text for time metaphors and the outcomes of the workplace cases.",
